Michael Hayden, a former NSA Director, has since acknowledged the concept of NOBUS:<p><pre><code>    You look at a vulnerability through a different lens if even with the vulnerability it requires substantial computational power or substantial other attributes and you have to make the judgment who else can do this? If there&#x27;s a vulnerability here that weakens encryption but you still need four acres of Cray computers in the basement in order to work it you kind of think &quot;NOBUS&quot; and that&#x27;s a vulnerability we are not ethically or legally compelled to try to patch – it&#x27;s one that ethically and legally we could try to exploit in order to keep Americans safe from others.&quot;
